Coffee Atlas is released under two licences, because it is two things.

SOFTWARE — MIT
    Applies to: the quality gate in scripts/, the GitHub Actions workflow, and the
    markup, styling and JavaScript of index.html (its structure, rendering logic,
    step generators and vessel drawings).

CONTENT — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
    Applies to: the coffee data and everything written for a reader — drink names,
    notes, ratios, doses, roast and grind guidance, brewing procedures, tips, origin
    notes, the English and Turkish copy, and the share card image (og-card.png).
    Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
    Summary:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    In short: reuse and adapt it freely, including commercially, as long as you give
    appropriate credit and say whether you changed anything.

